# Architecture & Plan Stratification

The reference for how to plan and execute changes in this Trabuco project.
The always-on rule lives in `CLAUDE.md` (and the equivalent agent rule
files); this document is the **how**.

## Why stratify

Trabuco modules form a strict dependency hierarchy. A multi-module change
that doesn't respect that hierarchy produces:

- Intermediate states that don't compile (Stage 1 broke the project; you
  can't run tests at the gate; you can't ship a partial PR)
- Reviews that fan out to unrelated areas (Module A's reviewer must
  understand Modules B-D to follow your change)
- Failure recovery that requires manual rollback (no clean rollback
  point per stage)

A stratified plan eliminates all three. Each stage is one module, the
project compiles cleanly at every stage boundary, and a stage failure
leaves the prior stages cleanly committable.

